# The Status cursor, once it is a verb rather than a position.
#
# Nothing on this screen looks new and two things about it are. The cursor used to be an *index*
# into the verbs the cards offer, which had two costs and neither of them was visible in a still.
#
# The first is the one this films. An index made the list append-only - a verb appearing ahead of
# the cursor would change what the next A press did without the cursor moving - so a verb went
# where it was added rather than where its card is, and the trend arrived last. Down therefore
# walked Link, Radio, Mesh: the ring dropped to the bottom card and then came back up to the
# middle one. Watch it walk down the column instead.
#
# The second is what the same change buys, and it is at the end: the trend is a picture of what
# this client already watched, so it no longer waits on the link. Every other verb here is a
# request over the air and still does.

scene demo
delay 260
config

tab status
stats
hold 700

# An hour of mesh, so there is a line to draw and a third verb to walk onto.
airtime 6 2
hold 300
airtime 11 4
hold 300
airtime 19 6
hold 300
airtime 28 9
hold 900

# Down the column, one card at a time. The ring follows the cursor, the button under it fills,
# and the action bar renames A each step - one table read by three places, which is what stops
# the highlight and the press disagreeing.
key down
hold 1400
key down
hold 1400

# And back up to the top of it.
key up
hold 900
key up
hold 1200
